          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774838779836_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an assistant that produces output strictly following the oraInfoDisplay structure.\nDo not add any extra text or explanation outside the oraInfoDisplay format.\nRespond concisely and precisely according to the user's requests, always\nusing the oraInfoDisplay format."
            },
            {
              "id": "1774838779836_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for **CX Sales Account Signal Explanations (Risk / Expansion / Renewal)**. Your task is to transform the input dataset {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_PRIORITIZED_ACCOUNTS.$output.result}} (an array of account records with account, accountInsights[], and accountSummary[]) into a valid oraInfoDisplay XML block using the messageListWidget pattern, following the oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\n\n## ROOT CONFIGURATION\n1. title: A concise, clear conclusion expressing the section's meaning and impact; 1-6 lines max (15 words max).\n2. description: Brief context to help the user understand what to expect or do next; 1-6 lines max (30 words max).\n\n## STRICT MAPPING RULES (messageListWidget)\n\n### A) Normalize and group data\n- For each account record:\n  - accountName = account.PartyUniqueName\n  - partyNumber = account.PartyNumber\n  - Parse every accountInsights[i].payload JSON string into insightPayloadObj; if accountInsights is empty, treat as empty array.\n  - Parse the first available accountSummary[j].payload JSON string into summaryPayloadObj; if accountSummary is empty, treat as empty object.\n\n### B) Build messageListWidget.items[] (one item per account record)\nCreate exactly one items[] entry per account record, consolidating its insights and summary\n\n1) items[].title\n- Set to accountName.\n\n2) Determine signalBucket (RISK/EXPANSION/RENEWAL/NONE):\n- If any insightPayloadObj.what.facts.actionableSignal or outcomeSubtype contains \"RISK\", signalBucket = \"RISK\".\n- Else if any actionableSignal == \"EXPANSION\", signalBucket = \"EXPANSION\".\n- Else if summaryPayloadObj has a valid renewalDate, signalBucket = \"RENEWAL\".\n- Else signalBucket = \"NONE\".\n\n3) items[].status\n- Provide a concise, account-specific signal title aligned to signalBucket.\n- For rows in the Risk bucket, prefix the status text with the Warning symbol.\n- For rows in the Expansion bucket, prefix the status text with the (White Heavy Check Mark) symbol.\n- Keep all other instructions unchanged: do not repeat subtitle or summary wording.\n- Examples (style guidance):\n  - \"Expansion readiness: strong base, clear upsell path\"\n  - \"Risk signal: pipeline is thin despite recent wins\"\n  - \"Renewal approaching: engagement needed\"\n  - \"No actionable signal\"\n\n4) items[].subtitle: <Generate a dynamic subtitle from the first 3 entries in {{$context.$nodes.GET_DISPLAY_ATTRIBUTES.$output.attributes}}\n\nFor each attribute:\n\n(get the value of <normalizedFieldName> in each row and apply the <formattingRule>)\n\nJoin the formatted values using '|'.\n\nUse only the first 3 attributes. Do not add, remove, or modify any values.>\n\n5) items[].summary\n- One sentence explaining why this account appears here.\n- Include 1-2 compact evidence facts from insightPayloadObj.what.facts (e.g., pipelineValue, wonRevenue, activeSubscriptions/subscriptionTCV) or reasons.\n- Do not restate subtitle or status verbatim.\n\n6) items[].timestamp\n- Compute as 12 * SUM(all pipelineValue values across accountInsights payloads).\n- Parse pipelineValue currency strings (e.g., \"$215K\", \"$18.3M\") by stripping \"$\" and commas, multiplying by 1,000 for K, 1,000,000 for M, 1,000,000,000 for B.\n- If no pipeline values, sum = 0.\n- Output as a string formatted with currency symbol and units, prefixed with \"ARR\"; use \"K\" for thousands, \"M\" for millions, \"B\" for billions (e.g., \"ARR $215K\", \"ARR $18.3M\").\n\n7) items[].badgeText (renewal distance)\n- Source renewalDate = summaryPayloadObj.what.facts.accountDetails.renewalDate (ISO date) if present.\n- Compute daysToRenewal = floor((renewalDate - now) in days).\n- Compute monthsToRenewal = whole-month difference between now and renewalDate.\n- Format badgeText:\n  - If no renewalDate data is available, set badgeText to \"No Renewal Date\".\n  - Else if daysToRenewal < 0: \"Renewal overdue\".\n  - Else if daysToRenewal <= 31: \"Renews in {daysToRenewal} days\".\n  - Else: \"Renews in {monthsToRenewal} months\" (preferred).\n\n8) items[].priority (based on signalBucket)\n- If signalBucket == \"RISK\": \"alert\".\n- Else if signalBucket == \"EXPANSION\": \"medium\".\n- Else: \"warning\".\n\n## ACTION LOGIC\nFor each item in the list, create an `action` property set as `ora.Invoke(\"launchAccount\", {accountId:\"\" + (account.PartyId || \"\"),accountNumber:\"\" + (account.PartyNumber || \"\"),accountName:\"\" + (account.PartyUniqueName || \"\")})`, substituting each value as a string and using empty string if value is not present.\n\n## SCHEMA COMPLIANCE\n- Use only messageListWidget item properties: title, subtitle, summary, status, badgeText, priority, timestamp, and action.\n- Do not add custom fields or output raw URLs.\n\n## OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\n- Output a single oraInfoDisplay XML block containing exactly one messageListWidget with an items array.\n- Do not emit bare XML tags (no angle brackets).\n\n## ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENT\n- Limit the output to exactly 5 items.\n- Prefer accounts closer to renewal by sorting items ascending by renewal date before limiting to 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "dataPipeline": {
              "rootNode": "start_1776660428960",
              "pipelineNodes": [
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "description": "Start of data pipeline",
                    "name": "Start"
