                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1776661527509"
                  },
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1779820328179_systemPrompt",
                      "name": "systemPrompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Return ONLY valid raw JSON that strictly matches the required array schema/contract.\n\nRules:\n\n* Do not use markdown.\n* Do not wrap the response in code fences.\n* Do not include explanations, comments, notes, prefixes, or suffixes.\n* Do not include any text before or after the JSON.\n* The response must be directly parsable by a standard JSON parser.\n* Ensure all property names and string values use double quotes.\n* Do not include trailing commas.\n* Do not return null unless explicitly allowed by the schema.\n* Preserve the exact response structure and field names defined in the contract.\n* If no records exist, return an empty JSON array: []\n"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1779820328179_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are the Account Prioritization Agent.\n\nAttributes for Prioritization:\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_ATTRIBUTES_FOR_PRIORITIZATION.$output}}\n\nAccounts:\n{{$context.$input.listOfAccounts}}\n\nPRIORITIZATION_RULES:\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_PRIORITIZATION_RULES.$output}}\n\nTASK:\nScore each Account using the prioritization rules. Use fields mentioned in Attributes for Prioritization output to assign the score. Treat missing expected fields as signal gaps.\n\nHard rules:\n\n* If Status is Closed Lost or Inactive, return priorityOrder 0 and priorityTier Low.\n* If ExpectAmount is missing or 0, return priorityOrder 0 and priorityTier Low.\n* Preserve the same order as Accounts.\n* Return one output object for every input Account.\n\nOUTPUT CONTRACT:\nReturn only a JSON array. Each object must contain exactly these fields:\n\n* PartyId: number\n* PartyNumber: string\n* priorityOrder: number from 0 to 100\n* scoreRationale: 2 to 3 concise sentences grounded in the provided data\n* recommendedAction: one specific next step for the rep, with a clear time horizon\n\nTIER MAPPING:\n\n* Critical: 80 to 100\n* High: 60 to 79\n* Medium: 35 to 59\n* Monitor: 15 to 34\n* Low: 0 to 14\n\nDo not return markdown, explanations, wrapper objects, extra fields, null values, topPositiveSignals, topRiskSignals, scoredAt, or any prose outside the JSON array.\n"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
